{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the territories are \"Puerto Rico\" (PR) and \"Virgin Islands\" (VI). The question says to exclude territories, so I need to sum the farmers_markets column excluding those two.\n\nLet me now create a build script that will:\n1. Read the farmers markets data\n2. Read the census data\n3. Filter out territories (PR and VI) from farmers markets\n4. Sum the total farmers markets\n5. Get US population\n6. Join them and calculate the ratio","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script to compute the metric, joining the two sources and calculating farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AcPWJoCXdnsBbWy6SftM7F","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_100k.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data\nfm = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"farmers_markets\", storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Read census population data\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census_population\", storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Filter out territories (PR and VI) and sum total markets\nfm_total = (fm\n    .filter((fm.state_abbr != 'PR') & (fm.state_abbr != 'VI'))\n    .aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fm.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nus_pop = (census\n    .filter(census.NAME == 'United States')\n    .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and compute the metric\nexpr = (\n    fm_total.join(us_pop, fm_total.k == us_pop.k)\n    .mutate(\n        markets_per_100k=fm_total.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000\n    )\n    .select('total_farmers_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":743,"cacheRead":17753,"cacheWrite":565,"totalTokens":19073,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0037150000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0017753,"cacheWrite":0.00070625,"total":0.00620855},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":111},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911807308,"responseId":"msg_011Ce73yDHPvTHjCWWcUw86c","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01AcPWJoCXdnsBbWy6SftM7F","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1373 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_100k.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911814787}]}
